   "claims": [
    "In essence, the lender helps the buyer pay the seller of a house, and the buyer agrees to repay the money borrowed over a period of time, usually 15 or 30 years in the U.S.",
    "In the U.S., the most common mortgage loan is the conventional 30-year fixed-interest loan, which represents 70% to 90% of all mortgages.",
    "Typically, mortgage lenders want the borrower to put 20% or more as a down payment.",
    "If the borrowers make a down payment of less than 20%, they will be required to pay private mortgage insurance (PMI).",
    "Borrowers need to hold this insurance until the loan's remaining principal dropped below 80% of the home's original purchase price.",
    "Most fixed-rate mortgages are for 15, 20, or 30-year terms.",
    "Therefore, the initial interest rates are normally 0.5% to 2% lower than FRM with the same loan term.",
    "For example, if a mortgage rate is 6% APR, it means the borrower will have to pay 6% divided by twelve, which comes out to 0.5% in interest every month.",
    "All 50 states impose taxes on property at the local level.",
    "With 52 weeks in a year, this amounts to 26 payments or 13 months of mortgage repayments during the year."
   ],
